From 387a407be43a592e6eb9f70832c81516a1c8d1e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:24:09 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 123/128] xwl, icon_manager: X11 dock-apps on the Dock and the
 Clip

X11 dock-apps (wmcpuload, wmclock, wmix, wmcliphist, wmshutdown...)
showed as nothing, or as small decorated windows, under XWayland. They
now show on a tile of the Dock or the Clip, as on Window Maker:

- A leader, told as Window Maker does (WithdrawnState, or the class
  "DockApp"), gets no window. Its WM_HINTS, WM_CLASS and _NET_WM_PID are
  read at the map request: wlroots reads them when the surface is
  associated, and most leaders never draw, so never get there.
- The tile shows the icon window if it is a top-level (libdockapp); the
  leader if the icon window is the leader itself or a child of it (the
  "wmgeneral" dock-apps draw the same image in both, and XWayland only
  gives top-level windows a surface).
- An icon window the program mapped before the leader (GTK dock-apps)
  is associated again, as the tile.
- The icon manager adopts the surface like the tray's layer surface:
  placed by the dock-app's name (WM_CLASS instance), dragged and removed
  as the other dock-apps; the X11 program gets the pointer, also the
  right button (the tile's menu is on the border); the X11 window is
  configured where the tile shows it, for its popups.

The original programs thus look and work as on X11. Tested with the 12
dock-apps of the Big WindowMaker X11 Dock and catalog in a nested
wlmaker (11 shown; wmix needs a sound card).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
